     <h1 class="title" title="Kullu Manali">Kullu Manali</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
     
     <p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Rohtang Pass , Manali Gompa ,Hadimpba , Rahala Falls,  Kothi,Jagatsukh, Vashisht, Solang Valley , Naggar , Manu Temple </p>

<p>Kullu and Manali are the charming <b>hill stations in Himachal Pradesh</b>. The snow covered peaks of majestic Himalayas on one side and <b>Beas River</b> on the other provides a flattering environment. The green carpeted valley of Kullu-Manali is a land of temples and the mountains inflame thrills in everyone.</p>
<h3>Manali</h3>
<p>Manali may be called <b>Switzerland of India</b>. The charm and <b>beauty of Manali</b> continues with the royal Himalayas and river Beas flows arrogantly through luxuriant valleys and apple orchards. The visitors loose themselves in the breathtaking ambience. The well-defined snow capped peaks; the crystal clear water of Beas River, deodar and pine trees, tiny fields and fruit orchards illustrates the wondrous canvas of nature to trekkers and honeymooners as well. The hill station 40 km north of Kullu valley is covered with grassy meadows carpeted with brightly colored wild flowers are site for enjoying the marvelous walks.</p>
<strong>Shopping at Manali</strong>
<p>The shops are flooded with Tibetian souvenirs, carpets and craft items.</p>
<strong>Sightseeing in Manali</strong>
<p>Though Manali is famous as one of the lands of temples yet there are many attractions for tourists. The <b>Dhoongri Temple</b> or <b>Hadimba Temple</b> dedicated to Hadimba, wife of Bhim, Manu Temple dedicated to Manu Rishi, club house on the bank of Manalsu Nallah, <b>Tibetan monasteries, Mountaineering Institute training</b> in <b>trekking, mountaineering, skiing and water sports, Nehru Kund, Solang Valley, Rahala Water falls, Rohtang Pass, Arjun Cave</b> and <b>Jagatsukh</b> etc. are the places to see.</p>
<h3>Kullu</h3>
<p>The charming and beautiful <b>Kullu valley</b> spreads to 80kms around river Beas. The dreamland has the streams encompassing the glens and mossy meadows and meander east to west welcomes the tourists, trekkers, mountaineers and painters to fly away from the heat & dust of the plains. The fresh air of the Himalayas invigorates the visitor. The scenic mountain is awesome.</p>
<p><b>Raghunathji</b> is the worshipped with great devotion by all the people of the valley. The <b>Silver Valley</b> celebrates <b>Dussehra</b> in a vibrant manner to show devotion to the reigning deity.</p>
<strong>Shopping in Kullu</strong>
<p>The valley is famous for its exquisite variety of handwoven colourful shawls and kullu caps.</p>
<strong>Sightseeing in Kullu</strong>
<p><b>Bijli Mahadev temple</b> shimmers like a silver needle in the sun. Visitors can have panoramic view of Kullu and <b>Parvati valleys</b> from here. <b>Raghunathji temple, Vaishno Devi temple, Apple orchards and trout hatchery at Katrain, Naggar, Kasol, Manikaran, Jamlu temple at Malana, Basheshwar Mahadev temple at Bajaura, Larji</b> and Banjar famed for trout fishing are some of the place that you must see.</p>
<h3>Adventuring options in Kullu Manali</h3>
<strong>Trekking</strong>
<p>Trekking in Kullu, Parbati, Lahaul and Spiti idyllic side valleys lead to Pir Panjal and Himalayan ranges. Popular treks in the Kullu Manali valley are - Raison-Malana-Chandra Khani-Raison / Manali-Bhrigu-Rohtang Pass-Manali / Manali-Chhika-Hamta Pass-Manali / Raison-Padri-Khauli / Pass-Garsa-Raison / Manali-Chandratal-Manali.</p>
<strong>Jeep Safari</strong>
<p>Jeep Safaris are exciting and give you an opportunity of having direct encounter with wild animals.</p>
<strong>Skiing</strong>
<p>The skiing slopes of Solang Valley, the splendid valley between Manali and Kothi and Gulaba slopes offers good skiing sites and visitors can witness the glaciers and snow-capped mountain peaks along with it.</p>
<strong>Whitewater River Rafting</strong>
<p>River Rafting on Beas stretching from Manali to Aut starts from Raison and Mohal points.</p>
<strong>Fishing</strong>
<p>River Beas is the perfect place for fishing. It is said that this river is abound with trout and salmon species of fishes.</p>
<strong>Paragliding</strong>
<p>Paragliding is structured by the local adventure companies in the Solang Valley.</p>
